# /download — a shareable link to the App Store. A real 302 rather than an HTML
# page so link previews in Messages and Slack resolve to the store's own card
# instead of a page that immediately leaves. No country segment: that resolves
# to the visitor's own storefront, where the /us/ form dead-ends outside it.
/download  https://apps.apple.com/app/id6791766677  302

# /p/<code> — every post short link is served by the one page, which resolves
# the code client-side and forwards to the App Store on anything that isn't a
# live post. 200 rewrite, not a redirect: the code has to stay in the URL for
# the page to read it back out of location.pathname.
#
# Destination is /p/ and not /p/index.html. Pages' clean-URL handling 308s
# index.html to the directory, so a rewrite aimed at the file lands on a
# redirect rather than an asset and falls through to the 404 page.
/p/*  /p/  200

# /u/<id> — a scanned profile code. Same 200-rewrite shape as /p/ and for the
# same reason: the id has to stay in the URL for the page to read it back out
# of location.pathname. Keyed on the user id rather than the handle because
# migration 076 made a freed handle reclaimable, so a printed code keyed on a
# handle could resolve to a different person later.
/u/*  /u/  200
